.vitest-cache/

# Working drafts stay local until someone deliberately publishes them.
#
# This repo is PUBLIC, and the convention is that plans, research notes and
# mockups get written here while the work is in flight — bound to a live
# review doc, not committed. At the time this was added there were 17 such
# files sitting untracked in the primary checkout, seven of them named after
# another project's ticket ids, all of them one `git add -A` from being
# public record forever.
#
# These patterns do NOT untrack anything: the plans and demos already in the
# repo stay tracked and their changes stay visible. What they stop is the
# accidental sweep. Publishing a new one is still available and is now a
# deliberate act — scrub it, then `git add -f <path>`. That is exactly the
# shape the "scrub the plan, then open a PR for it" task describes.
docs/product/plans/*.md
docs/research/*.md
# Tracked demos all live in demos/dev-server/ and demos/mockup/; anything else
# at the top level of demos/ is a one-off mockup for review, not a deliverable.
#
# Match everything and re-include the two real ones, rather than listing file
# types. The first cut used `demos/*.html` + `demos/*/`, and a symlink slipped
# through both -- `*/` matches directories, and a symlink is neither a
# directory nor an .html file. A symlink also carries its target path as
# content, so enumerating entry kinds is the wrong question here; the right
# one is whether an entry is something this repo ships.
demos/*
!demos/dev-server/
!demos/mockup/
